Move to the next unit when human-readable rounding reaches 1024.
make_human_readable_str() picks the unit while the value is at least
1024 and rounds the tenths afterwards, so a value just under a power of
1024 rounded up to 1024 of the smaller unit: 1048575 bytes printed as
1024.0K instead of 1.0M in du -h, ls -h, df -h and free -h. Carry a
rounded result of 1024 into the next unit.

---
 libbb/human_readable.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/libbb/human_readable.c
+++ b/libbb/human_readable.c
@@ -71,6 +71,10 @@
 			frac = 1;
 		}
 #endif
+		if (val == 1024) { /* rounded up to 1024: use the next unit */
+			val = 1;
+			u++;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return auto_string(xasprintf(fmt, val, frac, *u));
